        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 285.71,
          "end": 287.83299999999997,
          "en": "which has an error value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 289.26,
          "end": 292.40999999999997,
          "en": "Now If I do enter an invalid email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 292.40999999999997,
          "end": 294.99,
          "en": "which is not part of the database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 294.99,
          "end": 296.823,
          "en": "I get no user found.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 298.05,
          "end": 301.67,
          "en": "Now, if I do enter valid credentials though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 301.67,
          "end": 305.36,
          "en": "then we see that error now is null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 305.36,
          "end": 306.83,
          "en": "So, now we got no error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 306.83,
          "end": 308.58,
          "en": "Instead we succeeded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 308.58,
          "end": 311.373,
          "en": "And that is how we can sign a user in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 312.31,
          "end": 315.33,
          "en": "Now we can create users and log them in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 315.33,
          "end": 318.44,
          "en": "And we get this yes, no response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 318.44,
          "end": 322.67,
          "en": "What we're not doing yet though, is working with that token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 322.67,
          "end": 325.53,
          "en": "because of course in the front-end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 325.53,
          "end": 329.82,
          "en": "in our front-end components, when we get the result here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 329.82,
          "end": 334.82,
          "en": "we could now check if result error is falsey.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 334.85,
          "end": 338.43,
          "en": "Which means we have no error, which means we've succeeded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 338.43,
          "end": 342.31,
          "en": "And we could then set some auth state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 342.31,
          "end": 347.31,
          "en": "maybe also with help auth react context or a Redux",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 347.56,
          "end": 350.84000000000003,
          "en": "and use that state to change what we see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 350.84000000000003,
          "end": 354.33,
          "en": "for example to change the options in our header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 354.33,
          "end": 356.03,
          "en": "We could now do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 356.03,
          "end": 359.6,
          "en": "but whenever we reload that state would be lost,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 359.6,
          "end": 362.97,
          "en": "because we start a brand new single page application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 362.97,
          "end": 364.14,
          "en": "when we reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 364.14,
          "end": 366.39,
          "en": "All the state, which was only stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 366.39,
          "end": 369.89,
          "en": "in memory from the last visit would be lost.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 369.89,
          "end": 372.32,
          "en": "And that's not what we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 372.32,
          "end": 374.44,
          "en": "That's also not what we have to accept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 374.44,
          "end": 378.57,
          "en": "because that's exactly why we have this token concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 378.57,
          "end": 380.18,
          "en": "We can store that token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 380.18,
          "end": 384.86,
          "en": "in some more permanent storage than just our memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 384.86,
          "end": 389.07,
          "en": "And we can then also use that token to send requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 389.07,
          "end": 391.89,
          "en": "to potentially protected APIs,",
          "zh": ""
